cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Houses of Roman Timgad
message: If you use this resource, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Edher
    given-names: Kim
abstract: >-
  An open digital humanities project cataloging over a hundred houses excavated
  at Roman Timgad (Thamugadi, Algeria), and the lives lived within their walls.
  The project publishes the data behind a critical reading of provincial Roman
  domestic architecture, foregrounding veterans, workshop owners, and local
  Numidians rather than a single Pompeian template.
keywords:
  - Roman archaeology
  - Timgad
  - Thamugadi
  - domestic architecture
  - Roman North Africa
  - digital humanities
  - GIS
  - space syntax
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://timgadhouses.org
